---
title: Accessibility Statement
lastUpdated: August 2026
---
I am committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people of all abilities. This website strives to conform to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA standards.

### 1. Built-in Accessibility Features

This website includes a dedicated Accessibility Panel accessible via the floating accessibility button (wheelchair symbol) in the bottom-right corner:

- **Text Scaling**: Switch between Normal, Large (112.5%), and Extra Large (125%) base typography.
- **High Contrast Mode**: Enhances border lines, element boundaries, and text legibility in both light and dark themes.
- **Enhanced Reading Spacing**: Increases letter-spacing, word-spacing, and line height to assist visitors with dyslexia or visual processing differences.
- **Reduce Motion**: Instantly pauses background canvas animations and disables CSS transitions for visitors with vestibular sensitivities.
- **Link & Focus Highlighting**: Outlines and underlines all interactive buttons and links with high-visibility accent rings.

### 2. Technical Specifications & Usability

- **Keyboard Navigation**: All interactive components are fully focusable with visible focus rings (`:focus-visible`).
- **Semantic Structure**: Built with standard HTML5 semantic elements (`header`, `main`, `section`, `footer`, proper heading hierarchy).
- **Responsive Layout**: Fluidly scales across all screen sizes without loss of content or functionality.
- **Screen Reader Compatibility**: Includes appropriate ARIA landmarks, modal dialog roles, and descriptive alternative text for non-decorative media.

### 3. Continuous Improvement & Feedback

Accessibility is an ongoing effort. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement, please contact me directly at **contact@apostolosk.com**. I take accessibility feedback seriously and will make reasonable accommodations.
